WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.660
Is Thanos about to pull a Michael Myers and
come back for another film after his death?

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.540
According to a new report from We Got This
Covered, the Mad Titan made famous in the

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:13.240
Marvel Cinematic Universe by Josh Brolin could
be making a triumphant return in the next

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.040
MCU saga.

00:00:14.269 --> 00:00:18.199
The outlet cites an anonymous source that
claims Thanos will rear his massive purple

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:24.540
head once again in the, quote, "upcoming Annihilation
storyline" of the MCU which hasn't been confirmed,

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:25.040
mind you.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.420
There's also reportedly a possibility that
the intergalactic despot who died twice in

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.599
Avengers: Endgame once via beheading at the
hands of Thor…

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:33.900
"What did you do?"

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.380
"I went for the head."

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.880
… and later when Tony Stark used his own
take on the Infinity Gauntlet to snap past

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:47.510
Thanos out of existence will make a cameo
in The Eternals, popping up in sequences that

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:49.000
show him in his younger years.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:53.699
This could kick off Thanos' big return to
the MCU, with a brief appearance in the Chloé

00:00:53.699 --> 00:00:58.929
Zhao -directed feature, due out on November
6, 2020, leading into a more prominent presence

00:00:58.929 --> 00:01:03.280
in films that will tell the Annihilation story
and introduce the MCU to the villain named

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:03.780
Annihilus.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.160
"Forward!

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:06.640
And attack!

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.080
Destroy anything in your path!"

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.980
We Got This Covered expressed confidence in
its source and the information they have provided,

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:22.850
as the person or people claiming that Thanos'
return is on the horizon is the same source

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:26.840
that indicated Taskmaster would be the villain
in the forthcoming Black Widow movie.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.970
Based on the source's track record, one could
easily be convinced that Thanos is coming

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:32.280
back to the MCU.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.580
Rumors about Annihilus potentially joining
the Marvel movie world have swirled for ages

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:40.740
- does this mean that Marvel will actually
tell the Annihilation comics storyline in

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.000
the future and that Thanos will be a part
of it?

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.860
Written by Keith Giffen with editor Andy Schmidt
and a host of artists, Annihilation focuses

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:52.640
on many of the space-related characters in
the Marvel Universe as they face off with

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:57.520
Annihilus, an alien whose unquenched thirst
for conquest causes him to unleash the Annihilation

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.750
Wave onto the galaxy.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:03.220
Annihilus is responsible for the attacks in
the storyline and Thanos, with the guidance

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.860
of villains Skreet and Mistress Death, initially
forms an alliance with him.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:11.080
Eventually, though, Thanos decides to betray
Annihilus when he realizes he's planning to

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.400
wipe out all life in the universe.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.400
Hmm… where have we heard that one before?

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.080
"I know what I must do.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.870
I will shred this universe down to its last
atom."

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.880
Obviously, a lot went on in Annihilation,
and Thanos played an important part in the

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:28.380
action.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.500
It makes sense that if Marvel truly is planning
to introduce Annihilus and adapt the Annihilation

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.980
storyline for the silver screen, then Thanos
would return for those films.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.320
However, this all seems quite unlikely.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:41.790
Sure, Thanos could return to the MCU.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:46.520
Yes, Marvel can bring him back in Eternals
flashbacks, or a storyline set before the

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.340
events of Avengers: Infinity War and Avengers:
Endgame.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.880
And while the opportunity is certainly there,
the foundation for this idea is flimsy at

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:54.380
best.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.060
It's not a done deal that Thanos will actually
cameo in The Eternals, as We Got This Covered's

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.240
source simply said it's a "possibility."

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.260
Even if he does appear in the film, which
is plausible considering he is an Eternal

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:09.590
himself, there's no guarantee that he'll show
up in any other Marvel movie thereafter.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:13.730
Additionally, we know what Marvel has planned
for its Phase 4 films, and it seems that no

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:18.520
movie in that phase apart from The Eternals
will allow for Thanos to return in any noteworthy

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.900
capacity, if at all.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.600
Even when Phase 5 inevitably rolls around.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.720
there might not be room for movies solely
focused on the Annihilation storyline, with

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:31.530
the planned sequels to Black Panther and Captain
Marvel, Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3, and

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:35.440
possible X-Men and Fantastic Four projects
and don't forget about Blade!

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:41.190
That phase will probably launch movies in
2022 and 2023 to follow up the Phase 4 films

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:48.460
releasing in 2020 and 2021, meaning Phase
6 will likely play out in 2024 and 2025.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:52.960
By that point, several years after his potential
cameo in The Eternals, would anyone really

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.670
care about seeing Thanos making a legitimate
return to the MCU?

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.540
Maybe, but that's a long way off.

